# Profile: social
# Blocks mainstream social networks for BRICKED CLIENTS ONLY.
# Every other device on the LAN is unaffected by this file.
#
# Syntax: one bare domain per line. The controller expands each into
#   ||<domain>^$client=<bricked clients>
# which matches the domain and all its subdomains, for those clients only.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments. Blank lines ignored.

# Stop browsers resolving their DNS-over-HTTPS provider, which would let them
# bypass the Pi entirely. See doh-bootstrap.list for what this does and does
# not cover.
@include doh-bootstrap

# --- Instagram ---
instagram.com
cdninstagram.com
ig.me
                        # instagram.com covers i.instagram.com (the native
                        # app API host), so the app fails to load its feed.

# --- Facebook / Messenger ---
facebook.com
fbcdn.net
fb.com
fbsbx.com
facebook.net
messenger.com
                        # NOTE: whatsapp.com / whatsapp.net are deliberately
                        # NOT blocked. WhatsApp is commonly needed for family
                        # and emergency contact. Add them here yourself if you
                        # actually want messaging cut off.
                        # meta.com is also left out: it is corporate//login
                        # infrastructure and blocking it has odd side effects.

# --- TikTok ---
tiktok.com
tiktokcdn.com
tiktokv.com
tiktokcdn-us.com
byteoversea.com
ibytedtos.com
musical.ly
                        # ByteDance uses several rotating CDN domains. The
                        # ones above cover the current app; if TikTok still
                        # loads, check the AdGuard query log for the client
                        # and add what you see rather than guessing.

# --- X / Twitter ---
twitter.com
x.com
twimg.com
t.co
                        # t.co is X's link shortener. Blocking it breaks
                        # links shared FROM X in other apps too. That is
                        # usually desirable here, but it is a side effect.

# --- Reddit ---
reddit.com
redd.it
redditmedia.com
redditstatic.com
                        # redditstatic.com serves CSS/JS. Blocking it makes
                        # old.reddit.com render as unstyled text rather than
                        # failing outright, which is intentional friction.
